A||N||4||mad dog||Oil Pressure Gauge/Oil Light||||1||
Z||000000||mad dog||05-24-2000||12:53 PM||||86 SE V6 Oil Pressure Gauge jumps like crazy when at idle and will often trip oil light when coming to a stop (even at slow, slow speeds).  Sometimes car will almost stall or engine rpm will drop out too.  I'm concerned engine is getting starved of oil when light comes on.  Also, what's the best weight oil to use?  It seems to run better with 20W50, not the recommended weight.  I dont have any "real" tools to check on my own, so whatever you recommend has to be done by my mechanic--unless it's real easy.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||05-24-2000||01:03 PM||||It sounds like your oil sending unit is bad. It's located right side of engine kiddie corner from the battery. Check to make sure connector is clean and seated. If it is you can buy another sending unit and replace it. There is a chance the oil pump could be bad but more often it is the sending unit itself.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||05-24-2000||01:05 PM||||Wow that doesn't sound good.  If the pressure is in deed very low then the heavy 20w50 oil is whats keeping the engine alive.  5w30 is the recommended oil.  I'd check to see if the oil pressure is really that low.  IF it is you either have an oil pump about to fail, a bad oil pump drive shaft (between the distributor and oil pump), or a worn out engine.<P>Does the engine run alright at driving speed?  Any weird knocking noises?<P>Do you have an auto trans?  If so and you have problems with it stalling when coming to a stop you might look at the torque converter lock up solenoid.  Sometimes they stick and don't let the torque converter unlock on downshift.  This is like coming to a stop without putting in the clutch on a standard trans.  When the speed gets low enough the engine will die.  Do a search for this for info on how to check it out.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||05-24-2000||01:15 PM||||I may suspect the oil pump.  The V-6 was designed to use 5-30W oil.  When my oil sending units went (3X), the oil guage pegged at 80+ lb.  It did not drop to low pressure and trip the oil "idiot" light.<P>You are right to be concerned.<P>I vote with Carrolles.||||reg||3
Z||000004||mad dog||05-29-2000||11:10 AM||||Thanks for the info.  I'll see what I can do to correct the problem.||||reg||1
